## Linked issue

Refs nibiru-labs/openbot-roadmap#63 (M10 error handling, audit `docs/audits/openbot-errors.md`). Findings 1-9 and 11-15 are in this PR. Finding 10 is not fixed by decision: the released Team API codec rejects error codes outside its fixed list, so a code field needs a new versioned protocol.

## Type of change

- [x] Bug fix
- [ ] Small improvement or alignment, with no change to how a feature works
- [ ] New provider, MCP app, or connector
- [ ] Translation or documentation
- [ ] New feature or change to existing behavior (needs an approved issue)

## What changed

- `runCauseEffect` keeps the typed error tag, so the error reference and code reach the UI; agent error events carry a reference (1, 2).
- Team API routes forward only catalog text; other failures answer 500 without the raw message (3).
- An attachment import failure and a `shell.openPath` failure show catalog sentences; the operating system text stays in the cause (4, 8).
- Two provider status messages and the hourly provider update check use catalog keys and log failures with a code (5, 7).
- The hosted-site marker retry is capped with a backoff and reports once (6). The hosted server start retry stops after five attempts and shows the last failure in the host status (12).
- The tool router reports the cause of a failed tool call (9). A failed usage read is reported, not read as zero (13). A dead browser session shows when a CDP release fails (14).
- The remote-server classifier keeps refusals that are not 401 as `request_failed` (11); the preload decoder accepts that code (see risk).
- A failed queued message stores a catalog sentence in `error`, the redacted provider text in `errorDetail`, and an optional `reference`. Old rows keep their raw `error` and are localized when shown (15). No migration.

Surfaces: Backend, main (IPC handlers, remote server status), preload (one decoder value), renderer, `@openbot/i18n` (all locales), E2E scripts. No Team API wire change.

## Verification

- [x] Each fix has an E2E case or a changed E2E script (`failure-reporting-e2e`, `queue-delivery-failure-e2e`, `team-api-routes-e2e`, `backend-reliability-bounds-e2e`). Executor evidence: every run ended `done` with host verify rc 0 (`typecheck:node`, `i18n:check`).
- [x] Broad checks run in CI.
- [x] The pre-commit hook passed.
- [x] No credentials, private data, generated output, or real user files are included.

## Risk and security impact

**Trust boundary:** `src/preload/team-decoding.ts` gains one value, `request_failed`, in the list of server issue codes. Main already sends it; without it the preload decoder would reject the status. Sender validation and the other decoders are unchanged. **Data:** new queue failures add two optional fields (`errorDetail`, `reference`) to the stored delivery JSON; old rows are read unchanged and a downgrade still reads `error`. Secrets stay redacted before they are stored.

Model and harness: Codex gpt-6.1-terra, Cursor composer-2.5 and pi + MiniMax through openswarm; planner Claude Code.

